// =============================================================================
// 07: "TEXAS SHUFFLE" — SLOW BURNING 12-BAR BLUES (Key of D / Bm — 36 CPM)
// =============================================================================
// Simpler, slower, spacious 12-bar blues backing track in the Key of D / Bm.
// Layered in the intuitive performance build order: DRUMS -> BASS -> CHORDS -> ORGAN.
// Relaxed 36 CPM crawl tempo with calm single-heartbeat kick (zero nervous drum thumps).
//
// 🎸 HOW TO JAM OVER KEY OF D / Bm:
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// • D Minor Pentatonic + The Blue Note (Box 1, 10th Fret):
//    e |--------------------------------10--13--|  (D, F)
//    B |------------------------10--13----------|  (A, C)
//    G |----------------10--12-[13]-------------|  (F, G, [Ab = The Blue Note!])
//    D |--------10--12--------------------------|  (C, D)
//    A |----10--12-[13]-------------------------|  (G, A, [Ab])
//    E |--10--13--------------------------------|  (D, F)
//
// • B.B. King Sweet Box (D Major Pentatonic / B Minor Pentatonic, 10th-12th Fret):
//    e |--------10--12--|  (D, E)
//    B |--10-12---------|  (A, B) -> Bend 12th fret on B (B up to C#) for sweet blues cry!
//
// • Iconic Slow Blues Opening Lick in D:
//   Slow whole-step bend on 12th fret of G string (G bent up to A), hold with
//   heavy vibrato, release slowly to 10th fret G (F note), resolve to 12th fret D (D root)!
//
// 🎼 12-BAR HARMONIC ROADMAP (KEY OF D):
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Bar 1–4 : [D9] [G9] [D9] [D9]   -> Tonic with Quick-Change to IV in Bar 2
// Bar 5–6 : [G9] [G9]             -> IV Chord (Dig into crying bends!)
// Bar 7–8 : [D9] [D9]             -> Back to Tonic
// Bar 9   : [A9]                  -> V Chord (Peak emotional tension!)
// Bar 10  : [G9]                  -> Resolving IV Chord
// Bar 11  : [D9]                  -> Tonic
// Bar 12  : [A9]                  -> The Turnaround (Dripping tension back to Bar 1)
//
// 🎛️ CONTROLS (<leader> = Space in Neovim):
//   <leader>ml : :StrudelLaunch (Connect to Strudel engine)
//   <leader>mp : :StrudelToggle (Play / Pause backing track)
//   <leader>mu : :StrudelUpdate (APPLY CHANGES LIVE — Press after uncommenting!)
//   gcc        : Toggle comment on a line (1 tap to introduce/mute a layer)
// =============================================================================


// =============================================================================
// 🌧️ TRACK 1: "TEXAS SHUFFLE" (Slow 12-Bar Blues Crawl — Key of D — 36 CPM)
// =============================================================================
// PERFORMANCE BUILD ORDER: DRUMS -> BASS -> CHORDS -> SOMETHING ELSE (ORGAN)
//   Starts with DRUMS active laying down the deep, unhurried slow blues pulse.
//   Then layer by layer bring in your band:
//   Line 57: Boogie Bass | Line 60: Slow Blues Chords | Line 63: Hammond B3 Organ

stack(
  // 1. [DRUMS - ACTIVE] True 12/8 triplet shuffle cymbal (1 - a, 2 - a, 3 - a, 4 - a)
  s("[hh ~ hh]!4").gain(0.24),

  // 1. [DRUMS - ACTIVE] Deep wet hall snare backbeat on beat 3 only (authentic 12/8 slow blues)
  s("~ ~ sd ~").room(0.85).gain(0.65),

  // 1. [DRUMS - ACTIVE] Single soft heartbeat kick on beat 1 only (calm downbeat anchor, zero nervous thumping!)
  s("bd ~ ~ ~").lpf(190).gain(0.45),

  // 2. [BASS] Swung Blues Walking / Boogie Bass (Press gcc here)
  // note("<[d2 fs2 a2 b2] [g1 b1 d2 e2] [d2 fs2 a2 b2]!2 [g1 b1 d2 e2]!2 [d2 fs2 a2 b2]!2 [a1 cs2 e2 fs2] [g1 b1 d2 e2] [d2 fs2 a2 b2] [a1 cs2 e2 fs2]>").s("triangle").lpf(320).decay(0.6).gain(0.68),

  // 3. [CHORDS] Warm Slow Blues Chords (D9 - G9 - A9) (Press gcc here)
  // note("<[d3,fs3,c4,e4] [g2,b2,f3,a3] [d3,fs3,c4,e4]!2 [g2,b2,f3,a3]!2 [d3,fs3,c4,e4]!2 [a2,cs3,g3,b3] [g2,b2,f3,a3] [d3,fs3,c4,e4] [a2,cs3,g3,b3]>").s("triangle").lpf(1000).room(0.85).decay(1.4).gain(0.42),

  // 4. [SOMETHING ELSE - ORGAN] Hammond B3 Leslie swell (Press gcc here)
  // note("<[d3,a3,c4,fs4] [g2,g3,b3,f4] [d3,a3,c4,fs4]!2 [g2,g3,b3,f4]!2 [d3,a3,c4,fs4]!2 [a2,g3,cs4,e4] [g2,g3,b3,f4] [d3,a3,c4,fs4] [a2,g3,cs4,e4]>").s("sine").lpf(sine.range(700, 1500).slow(8)).room(0.9).gain(0.28),
).cpm(36)


